6. `build` → `BuildOwner`  ← registrationDate defaulted here
7. `assignHousehold` → `AssignHouseholdId`
8. `assignCode` → `AssignCustomerCode`  ← customer code (feeds membership number)
9. `assignNamesake` → `AssignNamesakeCount`
10. `save` → `SaveOwner`
11. `respond` → `RespondWithOwnerCreated`

All owner function classes live under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`.

## 2. registrationDate — defaulted to server date (NOT weekend-aware)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`
```java
13	    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
14	        Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(request);
15	        if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
16	            owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
17	        }
18	        built.set(owner);
19	    }
```
It is taken from the request if supplied, otherwise defaulted to `LocalDate.now()`. **There is no business-day / weekend roll-forward here** — it uses the raw calendar date. The field is stored on `Owner` at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java:54-55` (getter/setter lines 101-107).

Important discrepancy: the acceptance test (see section 5) asserts the default `registrationDate` is never Saturday/Sunday, and `AcceptanceBase` has a `toBusinessDay(...)` helper (lines 267-274) that also skips pinned `HOLIDAYS` (lines 240-242). `BuildOwner` does not currently implement this roll-forward, so this is where a business-day rule would need to be added.

## 3. Membership number + year segment

The membership number is a **derived DTO field computed in the MapStruct mapper**, not stored on the entity.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`
```java
26	    @Mapping(target = "membershipNumber",
27	        expression = "java(owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" "
28	            + "+ String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100))")
```
So `membershipNumber = <customerCode>-M<YY>` where the **year segment `YY` is the last two digits of `registrationDate.getYear()`** (zero-padded to 2). This runs in `toOwnerDto(...)` (line 36), i.e. on the GET/response path. Note it will NPE if `registrationDate` is null — it relies on BuildOwner's defaulting.

The `customerCode` prefix comes from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`:
```java
17	    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
...
27	        owner.setCustomerCode(String.format("%s-%s-%04d", city3, last3, sequence));
```
Format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (city 3-letter, lastName 3-letter, per-city 4-digit sequence = count of existing owners in that city + 1).

Also mapped nearby: `membershipTier` (line 29-31, SILVER/BRONZE from namesakeCount+email) and `locality` (line 32-35).

## 4. Daily create-limit enforcement

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RequireDailyOwnerLimit.java`
```java
17	    private static final int DAILY_LIMIT = 100;
18	
19	    public void service(OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws DailyOwnerLimitExceededException {
20	        LocalDate today = LocalDate.now();
21	        int count = 0;
22	        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
23	            if (today.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate())) {
24	                count++;
25	            }
26	        }
27	        if (count >= DAILY_LIMIT) {
28	            throw new DailyOwnerLimitExceededException(today);
29	        }
30	    }
```
Counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`; throws at 100+.

Supporting files:
- Exception: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.java` (checked, extends `Exception`).
- Handler: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DailyOwnerLimitExceededExceptionHandler.java` — responds HTTP 429 with body `{"errors":["registrationDate"]}` (lines 18-22).
- Escalation wiring: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.yml`.

Note: the counting uses `today` (raw now), consistent with BuildOwner's raw default — if a business-day roll is added to BuildOwner, this counter must roll too, or the two will disagree.

## 5. Related tests

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`
```java
14	    @Test
15	    void coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay() throws Exception {
16	        int id = createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
17	        DayOfWeek dow = LocalDate.parse(fetchOwner(id).get("registrationDate").asText()).getDayOfWeek();
18	        assertTrue(dow != DayOfWeek.SATURDAY && dow != DayOfWeek.SUNDAY, dow.toString());
19	    }
```
This is the only active assertion test, and it targets the business-day invariant for the default registrationDate.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — the black-box test harness (all tests hit `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`). Relevant helpers for your edits:
- `createMany(int n)` (lines 183-187) — creates n owners dated today, for per-day limit tests.
- `fillCity(city, n)` (lines 173-179) — per-city capacity.
- `toBusinessDay(LocalDate)` (lines 267-274) — weekend + holiday roll-forward reference.
- `HOLIDAYS` set (lines 240-242) — pinned 2026 public holidays the roll should skip.
- `shaHex`, `luhn`, `sha256hex` (lines 282-321) — reference algorithms for derived codes.
- Note class-level `@Transactional` rollback (line 49) and `@WithMockUser` admin (line 50).

There is also `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` (audit support, not directly registration-date/limit related).

One cross-cutting observation for editing: the test suite and `AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay`/`HOLIDAYS` expect a business-day-adjusted default registration date, but `BuildOwner` currently sets a plain `LocalDate.now()`. Aligning them means adding the roll-forward in `BuildOwner` and keeping `RequireDailyOwnerLimit` and the `OwnerMapper` year-segment consistent with whatever date `BuildOwner` produces.

